<article class="env-lemma" id="0FYC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FYC">Lemma <span data-tag="0FYC">57.5.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme proper over a field $k$. Let $K \in D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and let $E$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ be perfect. Then $\sum _{i \in \mathbf{Z}} \dim _ k \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_ X(E, K) < \infty $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows for example by combining Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0D0D" data-tag="0D0D">36.11.7</a> and <a href="/tag/09M4" data-tag="09M4">36.13.5</a>. Alternative proof: combine Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0FXU" data-tag="0FXU">36.11.6</a> and <a href="/tag/08E2" data-tag="08E2">36.11.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>